  "body": "Apparently `document.cookie` supports cookies with no value via `document.cookie = \"foo\"`. This is distinct on the wire (i.e. in the resulting HTTP headers) from cookies with value empty string (`document.cookie = \"foo=\"`).\n\nIs support for this needed, so that this API encompasses the entire cookie data model, or can we be stricter?\n\nRelated: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/804\n",
